        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900"><strong>Takes effect TBD.</strong> This is version 2.2 of the Terms of Service. Until then, version 2.1 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/terms" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 2.1</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Version:</strong> 2.2</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Subject to §12, by accessing or using any services provided by BreederHQ LLC ("BreederHQ," "we," "us," or "our"), including but not limited to the BreederHQ platform, marketplace, and client portal (collectively, the "Services"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, do not access or use the Services.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Version 2.2 of these Terms becomes binding on you only when the notice, effective-date, and affirmative-acceptance requirements in §12 are satisfied. Accessing or using the Services, listing, or taking part in a transaction does not by itself accept version 2.2.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ LLC is a Kansas limited liability company.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in these Terms have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1A. Geographic Availability</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">1A.1 Current Service Area</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services are currently available to users located in the United States only. BreederHQ reserves the right to expand or restrict its service area at any time, at its sole discretion.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">1A.2 International Access</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Users outside the United States may browse public marketplace listings but may not create accounts, complete transactions, or access authenticated features of the Services. BreederHQ may offer an international waitlist to notify interested users when the Services become available in their region. Joining the waitlist does not create any obligation on the part of BreederHQ to expand into any specific country or region.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">1A.3 User Compliance</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Users are responsible for ensuring their use of the Services complies with all applicable laws in their jurisdiction. The availability of the Services in a given region does not constitute an offer or solicitation in any jurisdiction where such offer or solicitation would be unlawful.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Nature of the Platform</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Technology Platform Only</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ is a technology platform that provides tools and infrastructure enabling animal breeders and animal-service professionals ("Providers") to manage their operations and connect with potential buyers ("Buyers"). Only breeders, through a breeder account, may list animals for sale or placement; a service-provider account lists services only (§3.1). <strong>BreederHQ is not a party to any transaction between Providers and Buyers.</strong></p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ is an introduction venue, not a party to any sale or service.</strong> BreederHQ introduces Buyers to Providers. It does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce the price, terms, conditions, warranties, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, delivery, or outcome of any agreement between a Provider and a Buyer, and it is not a party to that agreement. The Provider and the Buyer own their transaction and every dispute about it. A listing, storefront, message, waitlist, booking, invoice, payment request, or other feature of the Services that displays or records a term a Provider or Buyer has set does not make that term BreederHQ's. The same applies to BreederHQ's contract tools, as §7C.6 describes. BreederHQ writes the sample language in its contract templates, but a template term becomes a term of an agreement only when a Provider chooses it, edits it as the Provider sees fit, and adopts it as the Provider's own term with its Buyer; it is not BreederHQ's term, BreederHQ does not set or approve it, and it is not legal advice (§7C.1).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 No Agency or Brokerage</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Does NOT sell animals or services;</li><li>Does NOT act as a broker or intermediary in transactions (introducing a Buyer to a Provider does not make BreederHQ either), and acts as an agent only as expressly provided in §2.7 (Limited Payments Agent);</li><li>Does NOT provide escrow services;</li><li>Does NOT act as an escrow agent and does NOT hold any User's funds in trust or as a fiduciary; BreederHQ's own role in payments is limited as described in §2.3;</li><li>Does NOT guarantee, warrant, or certify any animals, services, or transactions;</li><li>Does NOT verify, endorse, or take responsibility for Provider listings, claims, or representations, other than displaying the passthrough results described in §2.5 (Third-Party Registry Passthrough) and §2.6 (Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough), each of which reports a third party's result and is not BreederHQ's verification, endorsement, or warranty;</li><li>Does NOT evaluate, validate, or warrant the authenticity, currency, or contents of any document any Provider uploads through the Services, regardless of whether such document is displayed publicly or linked from a Provider listing; and</li><li>Does NOT broker, recommend, evaluate, hold, escrow, verify, or facilitate any insurance coverage of any Provider; the maintenance of any insurance coverage by a Provider is solely the Provider's independent legal responsibility under applicable law.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.3 Direct Party Transactions</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All transactions conducted through or in connection with the Services are directly between the Provider and the Buyer. BreederHQ provides the technological infrastructure for the Services, including listing management, communication, and, where §2.7 applies, limited payment collection as the Provider's agent.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ's own role in payments.</strong> BreederHQ's role in payments is limited to the following: (a) charging Users, through its third-party payment processor, for BreederHQ's own subscriptions and fees, for which BreederHQ is the seller; (b) supplying software through which Providers request, accept, record, and refund payments from Buyers, which are made to the Provider and processed by the payment processor under its terms; and (c) where a payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, acting as the Provider's limited payments agent as described in §2.7. In none of these roles does BreederHQ decide whether a payment, deposit, reservation fee, or refund is owed between a Provider and a Buyer, hold funds in escrow or trust, or become a party to their transaction. The Marketplace Transaction Terms describe payment processing for Marketplace transactions in more detail.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.4 Meaning of "Verification" on the Services</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Other than displaying a Third-Party Registry Passthrough under §2.5 or a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough under §2.6, each of which reports a third party's result and is not BreederHQ's own verification or warranty, BreederHQ does not "verify," "vet," "certify," "endorse," "screen," "approve," "validate," or "warrant" any Provider, Provider claim, Provider credential, Provider document, or animal listed on the Services. Where the Services display any badge, indicator, or descriptor concerning a Provider, the display reflects (a) facts about the Provider's account history on the Services (such as date of account creation, response time to Buyer inquiries, dispute history), (b) the Provider's own representations and uploaded materials, (c) a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough as defined in §2.6, or (d) a Third-Party Registry Passthrough as defined in §2.5. <strong>No such badge, indicator, or descriptor constitutes BreederHQ's evaluation, endorsement, or warranty of the Provider's identity (including where a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough is displayed under §2.6, which is not BreederHQ's warranty), competence, fitness, qualifications, character, professional credentials, insurance status, licensing status, or the accuracy or authenticity of any Provider-uploaded document.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.5 Third-Party Registry Passthrough</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a public third-party registry operated by an issuing body (such as the American Farrier's Association, American Kennel Club, Orthopedic Foundation for Animals, or a state veterinary licensing board) maintains a publicly searchable record and returns a matching record for a Provider's Credential Attestation, BreederHQ may display an indicator labeled "Confirmed via [registry name] registry" together with a hyperlink to the source record and a timestamp showing the date of BreederHQ's query. Such display means only that, as of the timestamp shown adjacent to the indicator, the named registry returned a matching record in response to BreederHQ's query. <strong>BreederHQ does not undertake any duty to monitor the named registry for subsequent changes, withdrawals, expirations, or amendments. The consumer is directed to follow the hyperlink to the registry's source record as the authoritative source.</strong> If BreederHQ ceases to display a passthrough indicator, no inference is to be drawn as to the Provider's standing with the registry.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.6 Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a Third-Party Identity Verification Provider (as of the effective date of these Terms, Stripe Identity, operated by Stripe, Inc.) returns a successful identity verification for a User, such as the individual designated for a Provider's account under subsection (a), BreederHQ may display an indicator such as "Identity Confirmed," attributed to the named provider (for example, "Identity confirmed via [provider name]"), together with the date of the verification where that date is available. Such display means only that, as of the date shown, the named Third-Party Identity Verification Provider returned a successful verification in response to BreederHQ's request. <strong>The identity verification is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider in accordance with that provider's procedures, terms, and applicable law; BreederHQ does not itself perform the identity verification.</strong> BreederHQ does not undertake any duty to monitor the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider for subsequent changes to the User's identity-verification status. If BreederHQ ceases to display an identity-verification passthrough indicator, no inference is to be drawn as to the User's standing with the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) Identity check required to publish.</strong> Except as provided at the end of this subsection, passing an identity check performed by a Third-Party Identity Verification Provider (the "Identity Check") is a condition of publishing any listing, storefront, or service on the Marketplace. A Provider may not publish, or make publicly visible on the Services, any animal listing, breeding-service listing, storefront, or service listing until the individual BreederHQ designates for the Provider's account (the "Designated Individual") has passed the Identity Check. Where the Provider is an individual, the Designated Individual is the Provider. Where the account belongs to a breeding program, business, or other organization, BreederHQ designates the individual (as of the effective date of these Terms, the account's owner, the "Account Owner"). "Designated Individual" and "Account Owner" are further defined in the Legal Definitions Schedule. As of the effective date of these Terms, the Identity Check asks the Designated Individual to submit an image of a government-issued photo identification document and a live photo of their face directly to the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, which compares them under its own procedures. The Designated Individual must complete the Identity Check personally and submit only their own genuine identification and their own live photo. Before the Identity Check begins, BreederHQ will ask the Designated Individual to consent to it, and the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider may ask for its own consent. Only the Designated Individual may give that consent; no one else may consent on their behalf, including a person who accepted these Terms for the Provider's account. If the Designated Individual does not consent, the Identity Check does not proceed and the condition in this subsection is not met. A listing, storefront, or service that was already public when this requirement first applied to its Provider may remain public unless and until BreederHQ withdraws it under subsection (b); keeping it public is not a breach of this Section.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) Enforcement.</strong> BreederHQ may decline to publish, and may withdraw from public view, any listing, storefront, or service of a Provider whose Designated Individual has not passed the Identity Check. BreederHQ may set a transition period for listings, storefronts, and services that were already public before this requirement applied to them, and BreederHQ is not obligated to withdraw any of them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) What a passed Identity Check means.</strong> The Identity Check is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, not by BreederHQ, and any display of its result on the Services is a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough. A passed result means only that, as of the date of the result, the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider reported that the individual who completed the Identity Check for the account passed its document and live-photo checks. <strong>A passed result is not BreederHQ's verification, vetting, screening, approval, certification, or endorsement of any Provider, and BreederHQ does not vouch for or guarantee any Provider, animal, service, listing, or Transaction because an Identity Check was passed.</strong> A passed result does not establish a Provider's business name, authority to sell or offer services, licensing, credentials, competence, honesty, or compliance with law; the existence, health, ownership, or condition of any animal; that the individual who passed the Identity Check is the person a Buyer is dealing with; or that the account has not since been transferred, shared, or misused. Nothing in §2.4 or this Section makes BreederHQ a guarantor of any Provider's identity. BreederHQ does not keep the identification document, the live photo, or the details read from them after the result is recorded (subsection (d)), and it cannot provide them, or any other identity details from the Identity Check, to a Buyer or any other User. A passed Identity Check is not a means for a Buyer to identify, locate, or pursue a Provider. The presence of a listing, storefront, or service on the Services is not by itself a representation that its Provider passed the Identity Check: some that were public before this requirement applied may remain public without the indicator described in this Section. The presence of the indicator is not an endorsement, and its absence is not an accusation. Each Buyer remains responsible for the due diligence described in §3.2.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(d) Information submitted for the Identity Check.</strong> The Third-Party Identity Verification Provider collects and processes the identification document and live photo under its own terms and privacy policy. BreederHQ's systems receive the result, not the identification document image or the live photo. As soon as the result is recorded, BreederHQ has the images and identity details deleted from its account with the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider and keeps only whether the check passed, the check's reference number, and its date (a reason a check did not pass may also appear for a short time in BreederHQ's operational logs and error reports). Anything the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider itself keeps is governed by its own policies. The Privacy Policy describes this in detail.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(e) No alternative to the Identity Check.</strong> BreederHQ does not review identification documents itself and does not offer a manual review, an accommodation alternative, or any other way to satisfy the condition in subsection (a). If the Designated Individual cannot or will not complete the Identity Check, for any reason, the Provider's listings, storefront, and services cannot be newly published on the Marketplace, and any that remain public under subsection (a) may be withdrawn under subsection (b). The Provider's remedy is to cancel, with a refund of the unused prepaid portion of the affected fees, as provided in §2.3 of the Breeder/Seller Agreement and §2.5 of the Service Provider Agreement.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.7 Limited Payments Agent</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To the extent any payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, each Provider appoints BreederHQ as its limited agent solely for the purpose of receiving and settling amounts paid by Buyers for that Provider's transactions.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>A payment actually received by BreederHQ through the Services is deemed received by the Provider and discharges the Buyer's payment obligation to the Provider to that extent, whether or not BreederHQ remits that payment to the Provider.</strong> A payment that is declined, not successfully collected, refunded, reversed, or charged back is not a payment actually received for purposes of this Section, and the Buyer's underlying obligation to the Provider is correspondingly revived to the extent of the reversal.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ's sole obligation with respect to amounts routed through its payment infrastructure is to settle them to the Provider in accordance with these Terms, net of amounts recoverable under §6.4 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and the Provider's exclusive remedy for a failure to settle is payment of the unsettled amount.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ's role as limited payments agent is solely that of the Provider's payment collection agent; it does not make BreederHQ a party to any transaction and does not create any fiduciary, trust, or escrow relationship beyond that limited agency.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.8 No Duty to Mediate</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ has no duty to mediate, investigate, arbitrate, decide, or otherwise resolve any dispute between Users. Any help BreederHQ chooses to give, such as passing along a message, providing records it holds, or acting on a report, is voluntary, may stop at any time, does not make BreederHQ a party to the dispute, and creates no obligation to help again or to reach any particular outcome. Action BreederHQ takes to enforce its own User Agreements, such as removing a listing or suspending an account, is not a decision of a dispute between Users and does not affect their rights against each other.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. User Responsibilities</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Provider Responsibilities</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Providers are solely responsible for:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Accuracy and truthfulness of all listing information;</li><li>Never listing, advertising, or offering an animal for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit, in any form, from a service-provider account. Animals are listed only by breeders through a breeder account under the Breeder/Seller Agreement, and a Provider that both offers services and sells animals uses a breeder account for the animal sales. Listing animals from a service-provider account violates these Terms and the Acceptable Use Policy, and BreederHQ may remove the listing and suspend or terminate the account;</li><li>Passing the Identity Check required by §2.6 before publishing any listing, storefront, or service on the Marketplace (subject to §2.6(a) for one already public when the requirement first applied), and never describing a passed Identity Check as BreederHQ's verification, vetting, approval, or endorsement;</li><li>Compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local laws regarding animal breeding, sales, welfare, and any services the Provider offers;</li><li>Health, welfare, and condition of all animals in the Provider's care;</li><li>Fulfillment of all commitments made to Buyers;</li><li>Handling refunds, disputes, and returns directly with Buyers;</li><li>Obtaining and maintaining all licenses, permits, certifications, and qualifications required by applicable law for the Provider's operations, profession, and jurisdiction;</li><li>Maintaining all insurance coverage required by applicable federal, state, and local law for the Provider's operations, profession, and jurisdiction; BreederHQ does not impose, require, evaluate, verify, hold, broker, or facilitate any such insurance, and Provider's compliance with applicable insurance law is solely the Provider's independent legal responsibility;</li><li>Tax obligations that applicable law assigns to the Provider, as set out in §10 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Buyer Responsibilities</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Buyers are solely responsible for:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Conducting independent due diligence on Providers, animals, and services before entering into any Transaction;</li><li>Independently verifying all claims, certifications, credentials, and representations made by Providers, including by contacting the relevant issuing body, registry, or licensing authority where the Buyer wishes to confirm a credential;</li><li>Understanding and complying with applicable laws regarding animal acquisition, animal possession, and the receipt of services in the Buyer's jurisdiction;</li><li>Direct communication and negotiation with Providers;</li><li>Payment arrangements made directly with Providers;</li><li>Arranging transportation and receipt of animals or services.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Provider Attestations Regarding Credentials and Uploaded Documents</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A Provider may, through the Services, attest to professional credentials (including but not limited to certifications, licenses, accreditations, memberships, and continuing-education status) and may upload Supporting Documentation in connection with such attestations. By making any such attestation or uploading any such document, the Provider represents and warrants that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>the credential is currently held by the Provider and is in good standing with the issuing body as of the attestation date;</li><li>the uploaded document is authentic, unaltered, and was issued to the Provider by the named issuing body;</li><li>the Provider has not made any false statement to the issuing body or to BreederHQ in connection with the credential; and</li><li>the Provider will promptly update or withdraw the attestation and request removal of the uploaded document if the credential lapses, is suspended, is revoked, or is otherwise no longer accurate.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ does not open, read, validate, compare, evaluate, or vouch for any uploaded document. Display of an uploaded document or a link to it on the Services is not a representation by BreederHQ as to the document's authenticity, currency, or content. A Provider's false attestation under this section constitutes a material breach of the User Agreement and a violation of the Acceptable Use Policy.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Buyer Acknowledgment Regarding Displayed Credentials and Documents</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A Buyer who views or relies on any credential, badge, indicator, document, or descriptor displayed in connection with a Provider's profile or listing acknowledges and agrees that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>the credential or document was submitted by the Provider, not by BreederHQ;</li><li>BreederHQ has not opened, read, evaluated, compared, or validated any such document or claim; a passthrough display under §2.5 (Third-Party Registry Passthrough) or §2.6 (Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough) reports a third party's result and is not BreederHQ's evaluation, validation, or warranty;</li><li>the Buyer is solely responsible for independently confirming the Provider's credentials with the issuing body before relying on the credential for any decision;</li><li>the Buyer's reliance on a displayed credential or document is at the Buyer's own risk; and</li><li>subject to §4.3(c) and (d) and §10.5, BreederHQ disclaims liability for any harm arising from a Provider's misrepresentation of credentials or the inauthenticity of any uploaded document, except to the extent caused by BreederHQ's own conduct.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Disclaimer of Liability</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 No Liability for Transactions</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Subject to §4.3(c) and (d) and §10.5, BreederHQ expressly disclaims all liability for the following, except to the extent caused by BreederHQ's own conduct:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Any losses, damages, injuries, or deaths arising from transactions between Providers and Buyers;</li><li>The condition, health, genetics, temperament, suitability, or behavior of any animal;</li><li>Misrepresentations, fraud, or deceptive practices by any user;</li><li>Non-delivery, late delivery, or failed transactions;</li><li>Disputes between Providers and Buyers;</li><li>Any actions or omissions of Providers or Buyers, including the rendering of services by a Service Provider;</li><li>The authenticity, currency, or accuracy of any Credential Attestation, Supporting Documentation, or any document a Provider uploads through the Services;</li><li>The lapse, suspension, revocation, or expiration of any credential, license, certification, or accreditation a Provider has attested to;</li><li>The lack of, lapse in, or misrepresentation of any insurance coverage a Provider holds or is required to hold under applicable law.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 No Warranties</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. BREEDERHQ DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Limitation of Liability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) Excluded damages.</strong> TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, BREEDERHQ SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, OR USE, ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES OR ANY TRANSACTION CONDUCTED THROUGH THE SERVICES.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) Aggregate cap.</strong> TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, BREEDERHQ'S TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ALL CLAIMS ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO THE SERVICES, THE USER AGREEMENTS, OR ANY TRANSACTION CONDUCTED THROUGH THE SERVICES, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, STATUTE, OR OTHERWISE, SHALL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER OF (i) THE TOTAL AMOUNTS YOU PAID TO BREEDERHQ FOR THE SERVICES IN THE TWELVE (12) MONTHS IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING THE EVENT GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM, OR (ii) FIVE HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS ($500). This cap applies in the aggregate across all claims and does not reset with each claim.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) What this cap does not limit.</strong> Subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to BreederHQ's liability for: (i) fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; (ii) willful misconduct or gross negligence; (iii) death or personal injury caused by BreederHQ's negligence; (iv) BreederHQ's obligation under §2.7 to pay over amounts it has actually collected on a Provider's behalf and not settled, net of any amounts properly recoverable under §2.7 and §6.4 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms, provided that this subsection preserves recovery of those amounts in full and does not expand the exclusive remedy stated in §2.7; (v) BreederHQ's obligation to refund amounts charged to you in error; or (vi) any other liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited under applicable law.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(d) Consumer rights preserved.</strong> Nothing in this Section limits, waives, or otherwise affects any right or remedy that, under applicable law, cannot be waived as a condition of using a consumer service, including any right described in §10.5 (State-Specific Provisions). If any part of this Section is held unenforceable as to a particular claim or claimant, that part shall be severed as to that claim or claimant and the remainder of this Section shall continue in full force and effect.</p>
