        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7A. AI-Powered Features</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7A.1 AI Assistant and Scout AI</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services include optional AI-powered features ("AI Features"), including the AI Assistant and Scout AI, that use third-party artificial intelligence technology to answer questions about your data and the platform. AI Features are available to users with eligible subscription plans. The AI Assistant and Scout AI require explicit consent before first use. Other AI Features, such as contract import (§7C.3), the document-reading and drafting features, and Help Center search, send a document, information, or search text to an AI service provider only when you choose to use them; the Privacy Policy (Section 4.4) describes what each sends and which of them ask for separate consent. Every AI Feature that you choose to use follows the organization setting described in §7A.5. The one exception is a platform safety check that is not an AI Feature you choose to use: because Providers may not offer animals for sale on the Marketplace, our AI service provider reads the buyer-facing text of each Provider's Marketplace listings, and the Provider's public business name, business description, and service area, when a Provider registers, creates, edits, or publishes a listing or edits its public profile. That check runs for every Provider whether or not the organization has turned off AI Features, and a finding only flags the account for review by a person at BreederHQ (Privacy Policy, Sections 2.7 and 4.4).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7A.2 Data Processing Disclosure</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you use the AI Assistant or Scout AI, your queries and relevant summaries of your platform data are transmitted to our AI service provider, Anthropic, for processing. By consenting to use them, you acknowledge and accept this data processing. Help Center search, and the help-article searches the AI Assistant and Scout AI run, send search text to our AI search provider, Voyage AI. Other AI Features send what the Privacy Policy (Section 4.4) describes, and the Marketplace Provider listing screen described in §7A.1 sends the listing and profile text it names to Anthropic. Anthropic and Voyage AI handle what they receive under their own terms and policies. See our Privacy Policy (Section 4.4) for details about what data is sent, what is not sent, and how Anthropic handles your data.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7A.3 AI-Generated Content Disclaimer</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">AI-generated responses are provided for informational purposes only and should not be relied upon as professional advice, including but not limited to veterinary, legal, financial, or breeding advice. BreederHQ does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or suitability of AI-generated content. You should always verify AI-generated information independently and consult qualified professionals for important decisions regarding animal health, breeding, and business operations.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7A.4 AI-Assisted Content Displayed on the Services</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where the Services include features that generate text, images, or other content the Provider may publish to the Services (including listing descriptions, profile copy, or marketplace content), the Provider must review the generated content, edit it as desired, and explicitly accept the content as the Provider's own before publication. Content the Provider has accepted for publication constitutes Provider Content for all purposes under the User Agreements, and the Provider is solely responsible for its accuracy and compliance with the Acceptable Use Policy. <strong>A Provider may not publish AI-generated content the Provider has not reviewed and accepted.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7A.5 AI Feature Controls</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have the following controls over AI Features:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Organization administrators may turn off AI Features for all users in their organization at any time through Settings. That setting stops every AI Feature from sending data to an AI service provider, including the AI Assistant, Scout AI, contract import, the document-reading and drafting features, and Help Center search, which then finds articles by keyword instead. It does not stop the Marketplace Provider listing screen described in §7A.1, which reads only listing and profile text, never messages, private records, or documents;</li><li>Individual users may delete their AI interaction history at any time through the Help Center;</li><li>The AI Assistant and Scout AI require explicit consent before first use; you may withdraw consent by contacting us;</li><li>Disabling AI Features does not affect any other functionality of the Services.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7B. Third-Party Social Media Integration</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7B.1 Content for Third-Party Platforms; Publishing Only at the Provider's Direction</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services include features that generate platform-tuned text and image content the Provider may copy and paste to their own third-party social media accounts, including but not limited to Facebook and Instagram (collectively, "Third-Party Platforms"). BreederHQ may also offer a feature that lets a Provider connect a Facebook Page or an Instagram business account and publish content the Provider selects to it. If a Provider uses that feature, the Provider grants the connection through the Third-Party Platform's own authorization process, BreederHQ stores an encrypted access token for the connected account, and BreederHQ publishes only the content the Provider selects, when the Provider directs, within the permissions the Provider granted. The Provider may disconnect the account in the Services at any time. <strong>BreederHQ does not post to a Third-Party Platform on its own initiative, and a post BreederHQ publishes at the Provider's direction is the Provider's post.</strong> Any other post that appears on a Third-Party Platform was placed there by the Provider on their own account.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7B.2 Provider Responsibility for Posted Content</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Provider is solely responsible for any content the Provider copies, edits, or posts to a Third-Party Platform, or directs BreederHQ to publish there, including ensuring the content complies with that platform's terms of service, community standards, and content policies. The Provider acknowledges that Third-Party Platforms including Meta Platforms, Inc. ("Meta") restrict content related to the sale or transfer of live animals between private individuals, and that automated enforcement of those restrictions has resulted in account, Page, and content removals affecting many breeders.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7B.3 No Guarantee of Compliance or Account Safety</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ tunes generated content using guidelines designed to reduce the risk of automated enforcement on Third-Party Platforms, but <strong>no wording, image, or content is guaranteed to comply with any Third-Party Platform's policies or to avoid enforcement action.</strong> Third-Party Platform policies and enforcement systems are operated, maintained, and modified solely by those platforms and may change without notice.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7B.4 No Liability for Third-Party Platform Actions</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Subject to §4.3(c) and (d) and §10.5, BreederHQ expressly disclaims all liability for the following, except to the extent caused by BreederHQ's own conduct:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Removal, suspension, restriction, or termination of any Provider account, Page, profile, or content on any Third-Party Platform;</li><li>Loss of followers, reach, engagement, or business goodwill on any Third-Party Platform;</li><li>Changes to Third-Party Platform terms, policies, or enforcement systems;</li><li>Any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from a Provider's use of generated content on a Third-Party Platform, including content published at the Provider's direction under §7B.1.</li></ul>
