        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The first time a Provider chooses to generate content for a Third-Party Platform, BreederHQ presents a one-time disclosure summarizing the matters in this Section 7B. By continuing past that disclosure and by using the Services to generate content for Third-Party Platforms, the Provider acknowledges and accepts the responsibilities and disclaimers set forth in this Section.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7C. Contract Templates, Contract Preparation, and Electronic Signing</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.1 Scope; Templates Are Starting Points</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Section applies to every User who creates, customizes, imports, sends, receives, or signs an agreement through the Services, including a client portal User who does not use the Marketplace. In this Section, a "Transaction Contract" means an agreement between Users or between a User and another party prepared, exchanged, or recorded through the Services. It does not mean these Terms or another agreement between you and BreederHQ.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ supplies system templates, editing and data-merging tools, AI-assisted conversion, and electronic-signing tools as software conveniences. System templates are starting points, not legal advice or a determination of the terms appropriate for your circumstances. BreederHQ is not acting as your lawyer, and use of these tools does not create an attorney-client relationship. No template is warranted to be suitable, complete, or legally sufficient for any jurisdiction, species, transaction, or party. You are responsible for obtaining advice from your own qualified counsel concerning the terms you prepare or agree to; a User preparing or sending a Transaction Contract must arrange appropriate legal review before using it. The system templates and contract tools are not a substitute for the advice of an attorney.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Sample terms in system templates.</strong> BreederHQ writes the system templates, and some of them contain sample terms, such as health-guarantee periods and conditions, deposit, refund, and cancellation terms, limits on the seller's liability, and choice-of-law and court-location terms. Sample terms are illustrations of what a contract can say. They are not BreederHQ's terms, not a recommendation that any term suits a transaction, and not terms BreederHQ negotiates, sets, approves, or enforces (§2.1). A Provider who uses a template chooses which terms to keep, edits them, and adopts the result as its own terms with its Buyer. A sample term may not be lawful or enforceable where the Provider or the Buyer is located, and the law of a Buyer's state, including laws that protect people who buy pets, may give the Buyer rights that a contract cannot reduce or waive.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.2 Responsibility for Contract Content</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">As between BreederHQ and the User preparing or sending a Transaction Contract, that User is solely responsible for selecting and reviewing its content, wording, accuracy, completeness, legality, and enforceability, including system-template language the User adopts, custom clauses, imported terms, and merged data. Before sending, that User must verify the final rendered document, including the parties, animal identification, amounts, dates, conditions, and attachments, and correct any errors. Saving, rendering, sending, signing, or generating a PDF does not mean BreederHQ has reviewed or approved the contract for legal adequacy.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A recipient should read the entire Transaction Contract and obtain any needed independent advice before signing. A recipient's review or signature does not transfer the preparing User's obligations to the recipient or waive any mandatory consumer right. Each party remains responsible for its own representations, authority, and performance. Nothing in this Section makes a User responsible for BreederHQ's own conduct where applicable law places responsibility on BreederHQ.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.3 AI-Assisted Contract Import and Conversion</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">AI-assisted contract conversion can omit, add, or change language, formatting, meaning, and data-field mappings. It does not provide legal review, certify fidelity to the source, or update a document to comply with law. Before using an imported template or sending a contract made from it, you must compare the conversion with the source, review every clause and field, and verify the final rendered document. You remain responsible for content you adopt and send, including AI-produced content.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The accuracy and professional-advice limitations in §7A.3 apply expressly to AI-assisted contract conversion. This cross-reference does not represent that the importer has the AI Assistant's or Scout AI's consent screens or history-deletion tools; like every AI Feature, the importer follows the organization setting described in §7A.5. The importer sends uploaded PDF content, or converted document text for other supported formats, to Anthropic for processing. Do not submit material you lack authority to provide, and remove information unnecessary for conversion before uploading. This Section does not replace the Privacy Policy or authorize processing that applicable law prohibits.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.4 No Warranty of Validity or Enforceability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, BREEDERHQ DOES NOT WARRANT THE CONTENT, ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, LEGAL ADEQUACY, VALIDITY, BINDING EFFECT, OR ENFORCEABILITY OF ANY TRANSACTION CONTRACT, WHETHER BASED ON A SYSTEM TEMPLATE, AUTHORED OR CUSTOMIZED BY A USER, IMPORTED WITH AI ASSISTANCE, OR SIGNED OR RECORDED THROUGH THE SERVICES. BreederHQ does not warrant that any provision will achieve a party's intended legal or commercial result.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.5 Signing Tools and Records</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Services capture signature submissions and certain associated event data and can generate contract PDFs. The existence of a signature image, typed name, timestamp, IP address, device information, hash, audit entry, or PDF is not a certification by BreederHQ of a person's identity, authority, capacity, informed consent, intent, or the legal effect of the document. A hash relates to the particular data hashed; it does not by itself establish who signed, that every contract term was preserved, or that a record has an unbroken chain of custody. An uploaded signed document records what was submitted; it is not proof that BreederHQ witnessed its execution.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Electronic signatures and records can have legal effect under applicable law, but use of these tools alone does not establish compliance with the ESIGN Act, a state's electronic-transactions law, or transaction-specific formalities. BreederHQ does not certify that a Transaction Contract satisfies requirements for consumer disclosures, delivery, receipt, witnesses, notarization, or record retention. The party required by law to supply or retain a record remains responsible for doing so. Keep accessible copies of the complete agreement and associated records for the period applicable to your transaction; the Services are not a promise of indefinite archival availability.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Agreeing to sign a Transaction Contract electronically is distinct from consenting to electronic delivery of legally required consumer records. Where that delivery requires additional disclosures, consent, or an access demonstration, those requirements must be satisfied separately before relying on electronic delivery. A link or signature checkbox alone does not establish that they were satisfied. Nothing here requires anyone to accept electronic records where applicable law permits them to decline.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.6 Contract Disputes and Preserved Rights</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ's contract templates, editing tools, AI-assisted conversion, and electronic signing are tools that BreederHQ supplies. The parties to a Transaction Contract choose and own its contents. A template, including a template BreederHQ provides, is a starting point; it is not legal advice, not a recommendation that any term suits a transaction, and not a term of BreederHQ's. BreederHQ does not become a party to, legal adviser for, or guarantor of a Transaction Contract by supplying a template or tools to prepare, exchange, sign, store, or render it. Disputes between the parties about its drafting, wording, interpretation, validity, enforceability, performance, remedies, or outcome are for those parties to resolve. BreederHQ does not undertake to enforce a Transaction Contract, secure a remedy, or guarantee a dispute outcome.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To the maximum extent permitted by law, BreederHQ disclaims responsibility for losses to the extent caused by a party's selection or use of contract terms, inaccurate inputs, unauthorized representations, or failure to perform. Any liability of BreederHQ remains governed by §4.3, including its carve-outs and consumer-rights savings, and §10.5. This Section does not enlarge the liability exclusions or cap in §4.3, disclaim liability that cannot lawfully be disclaimed, waive a consumer's mandatory rights, or release claims for BreederHQ's fraud or willful misconduct. It does not eliminate BreederHQ's separately stated obligations concerning its own Services or payment-related activities.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7C.7 Prospective Application</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The provisions added in version 2.2 apply only to use of the contract tools after this version takes effect for you following the required notice and your affirmative acceptance, as expressly required for version 2.2 by §12. They do not apply to Transaction Contracts already executed before that time, release accrued claims, change the parties' existing contract terms, or retroactively supply consent or evidence. For a Transaction Contract already sent or partially signed before that time, the new provisions do not apply to the existing document or its remaining signatures. A later, separately agreed new contract is assessed on its own facts; merely viewing, downloading, or countersigning an existing document does not bring it under these new provisions. BreederHQ will not require you to accept these provisions as a condition of retrieving, viewing, or downloading a Transaction Contract you executed before they take effect for you.</p>
